       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and potentially life-threatening shock. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change that.\n\nThe usual adult dosing is:\n- **Starting dose:** 5 mg by mouth once daily. Some patients, such as frail or elderly patients, start at 2.5 mg.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg by mouth once daily.\n\n- **If 50 mg was a typo:** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily if you confirm which one the prescriber intended.\n- **If the dose is intentional:** The prescribing clinician should confirm it directly and enter or co-sign the order. A pharmacist should also review it.\n\nSince you aren't a clinician, the best step is to have the treating prescriber send the order, or to confirm the intended dose with them. I can enter it once I have a corrected dose or clinician confirmation."
